81
00:03:01,020 --> 00:03:02,980
and to give you much more accurate predictions

82
00:03:02,980 --> 00:03:03,920
of what's going on.

83
00:03:05,100 --> 00:03:07,380
All right, and the betting markets have applied

84
00:03:07,380 --> 00:03:08,380
to lots of different cases.

85
00:03:08,380 --> 00:03:10,860
So they've been used for internal markets,

86
00:03:10,860 --> 00:03:12,980
things like, I think Hewlett Packard for a while

87
00:03:12,980 --> 00:03:15,140
had an internal market where their employees could bet

88
00:03:15,140 --> 00:03:17,300
on which products were gonna be successful.

89
00:03:17,300 --> 00:03:20,460
So which divisions would be profitable, things like this.

90
00:03:20,460 --> 00:03:23,420
So Robin has two really big ideas,

91
00:03:23,420 --> 00:03:25,660
one huge and one ginormous

92
00:03:27,380 --> 00:03:29,780
for how to leverage betting markets.

93
00:03:29,780 --> 00:03:32,540
So he has one piece, I think in Forbes called,

94
00:03:32,540 --> 00:03:35,020
we should set up a fire the CEO market.

95
00:03:35,020 --> 00:03:36,900
And what this says is when you write the corporate charter

96
00:03:36,900 --> 00:03:39,980
for your business, you set up a betting market

97
00:03:39,980 --> 00:03:41,420
in two things.

98
00:03:41,420 --> 00:03:43,660
First of all, the value of the company stock

99
00:03:43,660 --> 00:03:45,980
if the current CEO does not get fired,

100
00:03:45,980 --> 00:03:47,380
and then the value of the company stock

101
00:03:47,380 --> 00:03:48,780
if he does get fired.

102
00:03:48,780 --> 00:03:50,600
And the corporate charter says,

103
00:03:50,600 --> 00:03:52,700
if that second value ever exceeds the first,

104
00:03:52,700 --> 00:03:54,000
he is automatically fired.

105
00:03:54,980 --> 00:03:56,380
It just is a matter of rule.

106
00:03:57,420 --> 00:04:00,180
Is there a way to corner the betting markets?

107
00:04:00,180 --> 00:04:01,960
Well, in theory, of course, there always is.

108
00:04:01,960 --> 00:04:04,420
So yes, the CEO could just try and go and try to buy it,

109
00:04:04,420 --> 00:04:09,420
but remember, anytime that there is an eventual realization

110
00:04:09,820 --> 00:04:11,460
of what happens in the world,

111
00:04:11,460 --> 00:04:14,020
then you can just go,

112
00:04:14,020 --> 00:04:15,300
especially as long as they're short selling,

113
00:04:15,300 --> 00:04:16,460
you can just go and sell it short

114
00:04:16,460 --> 00:04:17,700
and you can make a ton of money off of that,

115
00:04:17,700 --> 00:04:19,520
or in principle, you can make an infinite amount.

116
00:04:19,520 --> 00:04:21,620
So if the CEO is just trying to go

117
00:04:21,620 --> 00:04:23,900
and artificially inflate his price,

118
00:04:23,900 --> 00:04:26,500
but you're allowed to go and sell that stock short,

119
00:04:26,500 --> 00:04:28,660
you can just go and create a billion dollars worth of that

120
00:04:28,660 --> 00:04:31,140
and say either buy the billion dollars of it, CEO,

121
00:04:31,140 --> 00:04:34,180
or the price is going to become realistic again.

122
00:04:35,100 --> 00:04:36,140
All right, so anyway, that was the idea,

123
00:04:36,140 --> 00:04:37,940
was to go and leverage betting markets

124
00:04:37,940 --> 00:04:39,980
to go and tell companies when it's time

125
00:04:39,980 --> 00:04:41,580
to fire the CEO and try again.

126
00:04:41,580 --> 00:04:45,660
So that is a huge idea.

